.TH "splitlayout" 3tcl 0\&.1 "splitlayout" "splitlayout package"
.SH NAME
splitlayout - Commands in namespace splitlayout
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsplitlayout create OBJNAME\fP \fIpath ?-width width? ?-height height? ?-opaqueresize boolean? ?-sashpreview mode?\fP
.br
\fBsplitlayout new\fP \fIpath ?-width width? ?-height height? ?-opaqueresize boolean? ?-sashpreview mode?\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ destroy\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ children\fP \fIid\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ clear\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ container\fP \fIvalue\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ frame\fP \fIid\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ insert\fP \fInode ?-side side?\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ leaves\fP \fI?id?\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ locate\fP \fIpath\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ move\fP \fIleaf -left|-right|-top|-bottom|-before|-after target\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ node\fP \fIpath\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ parent\fP \fIid\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ proportions\fP \fInode ?weights?\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ ratio\fP \fInode ?value?\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ remove\fP \fIid\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ retain\fP \fIid\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ root\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ split\fP \fInode ?-orient orientation? ?-ratio fraction? ?-keep child?\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ swap\fP \fIa b\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ tree\fP \fI?id?\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ type\fP \fIid\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ widget\fP \fIid\fP
.br
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ widgets\fP \fI?path?\fP
.br
.SH SPLITLAYOUT
.SH CLASSES
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBsplitlayout\fR (::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Configurable TclOO layout manager for Tcl/Tk 9\&.
.PP
configure is inherited from oo::configurable\&. With no arguments it returns a dictionary
of property names and values; with one property name it returns that value\&. Set properties
with option/value pairs\&. Pairs are applied in order, and a failed setter leaves earlier
successful assignments in effect\&. Use configure -name instead of cget -name\&.
.PP
Hull properties delegate directly to the ttk frame\&. No option objects or option-database
resources are created for the layout properties\&.
.PP
\fBMethod summary\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
constructor
Constructor for the class\&.
.TP
destructor
Destructor for the class\&.
.TP
\fIconfigure\fP [URL: https://www\&.tcl-lang\&.org/man/tcl9\&.0/TclCmd/index\&.html]
Configure properties\&. See \fI::oo::configuresupport::configurable\fP [URL: https://www\&.tcl-lang\&.org/man/tcl9\&.0/TclCmd/index\&.html]\&.
.TP
children
Returns the immediate logical children of a node\&. Child identifiers in pane order, or an empty list for a leaf\&.
.TP
clear
Destroys all layout content and creates one empty root leaf\&.
.TP
container
Returns the geometry container for a managed node\&. The hull for the root, or the logical parent panedwindow for another node\&.
.TP
frame
Returns the content frame of a leaf\&. The leaf content frame pathname\&.
.TP
insert
Inserts an empty leaf beside an existing non-root node\&.
.TP
leaves
Collects the leaves below a logical node\&.
.TP
locate
Finds the leaf containing an application widget\&.
.TP
move
Moves an existing leaf to an edge or sibling position without destroying its content\&.
.TP
node
Finds the logical node associated with an exact widget pathname\&.
.TP
parent
Returns the logical parent of a node\&. The parent node identifier, or an empty string for the root\&.
.TP
proportions
Queries or sets all pane proportions of a split\&.
.TP
ratio
Queries or sets the first pane fraction of a two-child split\&.
.TP
remove
Removes a node and all content in its subtree\&.
.TP
retain
Keeps a node while removing its siblings and collapsing its parent\&.
.TP
root
Returns the current logical root node\&. The root node identifier\&.
.TP
\fIsplit\fP [URL: https://www\&.tcl-lang\&.org/man/tcl9\&.0/TclCmd/index\&.html]
Replaces a leaf with a split containing two new leaves\&.
.TP
swap
Exchanges the content frames assigned to two leaves\&.
.TP
tree
Returns a recursive snapshot of the logical layout hierarchy\&. A nested dictionary describing the requested logical subtree\&.
.TP
type
Returns the type of a logical node\&. The string leaf or split\&.
.TP
widget
Returns the widget associated with a logical node\&. The content frame pathname for a leaf, or panedwindow pathname for a split\&.
.TP
widgets
Returns a recursive snapshot of the actual Tk widget hierarchy\&. A nested widget dictionary with path, parent, class, manager, container, and children\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBProperties\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-borderwidth
Readable, writable\&. Hull border width, delegated to the ttk frame\&.
.TP
-class
Readable\&. Read-only hull class override; empty when the default ttk class is used\&.
.TP
-cursor
Readable, writable\&. Hull cursor, delegated to the ttk frame\&.
.TP
-height
Readable, writable\&. Requested hull height, delegated to the ttk frame; constructor default 600\&.
.TP
-opaqueresize
Readable, writable\&. Boolean enabling live sash resizing; default true\&. Values are normalized to 0 or 1\&. Changing the value cancels an active deferred drag without committing its target\&.
.TP
-padding
Readable, writable\&. Internal hull padding, delegated to the ttk frame\&.
.TP
-relief
Readable, writable\&. Hull relief, delegated to the ttk frame\&.
.TP
-sashpreview
Readable, writable\&. Deferred sash preview: window, inline, or none; default window\&. Changing the value cancels an active deferred drag\&. Invalid values preserve the old value\&.
.TP
-style
Readable, writable\&. Hull ttk style, delegated to the ttk frame\&.
.TP
-takefocus
Readable, writable\&. Hull focus traversal setting, delegated to the ttk frame\&.
.TP
-width
Readable, writable\&. Requested hull width, delegated to the ttk frame; constructor default 800\&.
.RE
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBconstructor\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Creates a split layout with one empty root leaf\&.
.RS 4n
\fBsplitlayout create OBJNAME\fP \fIpath ?-width width? ?-height height? ?-opaqueresize boolean? ?-sashpreview mode?\fP
.br
\fBsplitlayout new\fP \fIpath ?-width width? ?-height height? ?-opaqueresize boolean? ?-sashpreview mode?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-height height
Nonnegative requested hull height in pixels; default 600\&.
.TP
-opaqueresize boolean
Enable live sash resizing; default true\&.
.TP
-sashpreview mode
Deferred preview mode: window, inline, or none; default window\&.
.TP
-width width
Nonnegative requested hull width in pixels; default 800\&.
.TP
path
New, non-root Tk widget pathname\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
The hull is a ttk frame\&. Managed content frames and panedwindows are its immediate Tk children; their logical
layout hierarchy is stored separately\&. The object command takes the widget pathname\&. Existing widgets or
commands at that pathname, invalid sizes, and invalid options raise an error\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Nothing\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBdestructor\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Destroys the layout and all of its content widgets\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ destroy\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Cancels deferred dragging and pending geometry callbacks, removes the manager binding scripts and owner
bindtag, and destroys the owned hull\&. Also supports cleanup after partially completed construction\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Nothing\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBchildren\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Returns the immediate logical children of a node\&.
Child identifiers in pane order, or an empty list for a leaf\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ children\fP \fIid\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
id
Existing logical node identifier\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Returns the immediate logical children of a node\&.
Child identifiers in pane order, or an empty list for a leaf\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBclear\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Destroys all layout content and creates one empty root leaf\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ clear\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The new root leaf identifier\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBcontainer\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Returns the geometry container for a managed node\&.
The hull for the root, or the logical parent panedwindow for another node\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ container\fP \fIvalue\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
value
Logical node identifier or exact managed widget pathname\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
The container can differ from the actual Tk parent\&. Unknown identifiers and unmanaged paths raise an error\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Returns the geometry container for a managed node\&.
The hull for the root, or the logical parent panedwindow for another node\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBframe\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Returns the content frame of a leaf\&.
The leaf content frame pathname\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ frame\fP \fIid\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
id
Existing leaf identifier\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Raises an error if the node is unknown or is a split\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Returns the content frame of a leaf\&.
The leaf content frame pathname\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBinsert\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Inserts an empty leaf beside an existing non-root node\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ insert\fP \fInode ?-side side?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-side side
Position of the new leaf relative to node: before or after; default after\&.
.TP
node
Identifier of the leaf or split beside which to insert a sibling\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
The new leaf shares the target parent, and the target pane share is divided equally between the two siblings\&.
Inserting beside the root raises an error; split the root first\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The new leaf identifier\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBleaves\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Collects the leaves below a logical node\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ leaves\fP \fI?id?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
id
Subtree root identifier; empty selects the layout root\&. Optional, default ""\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Traversal follows pane order recursively\&. A leaf includes itself\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
A list of leaf identifiers in depth-first pane order\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBlocate\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Finds the leaf containing an application widget\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ locate\fP \fIpath\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
path
Widget pathname to locate\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Walks the actual Tk parent chain looking for a managed content frame\&.
A split panedwindow does not identify a leaf\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The containing leaf identifier, or empty for a missing or unrelated widget\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBmove\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Moves an existing leaf to an edge or sibling position without destroying its content\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ move\fP \fIleaf -left|-right|-top|-bottom|-before|-after target\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-after target
Insert after a non-root leaf or split in its existing parent\&.
.TP
-before target
Insert before a non-root leaf or split in its existing parent\&.
.TP
-bottom target
Place after a target leaf in a vertical split\&.
.TP
-left target
Place before a target leaf in a horizontal split\&.
.TP
-right target
Place after a target leaf in a horizontal split\&.
.TP
-top target
Place before a target leaf in a vertical split\&.
.TP
leaf
Existing source leaf identifier, retained by the move\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Exactly one destination option is required\&. Edge destinations reuse the target parent when its orientation
matches\&. Otherwise the target leaf becomes a split, and its existing frame moves to a newly identified leaf,
following split's identifier semantics\&. The source identifier, frame, widget paths, and state survive\&.
.PP
Within one parent and orientation, panes are reordered with their existing weights\&. Other moves divide the
target share equally between the source and target; remaining source siblings retain relative proportions\&.
A source parent left with one child is collapsed after insertion\&. Moving to oneself or to an already adjacent
position does nothing\&. Argument errors are detected before changing layout or cancelling a deferred drag\&.
A successful structural move cancels deferred dragging and rebuilds geometry once, without nested updates\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The unchanged source leaf identifier\&. Query parent, children, or tree for the resulting structure\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBnode\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Finds the logical node associated with an exact widget pathname\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ node\fP \fIpath\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
path
Managed content frame or panedwindow pathname\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
This method does not search ancestors; use locate for application widgets inside a content frame\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The node identifier, or an empty string when no node matches\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBparent\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Returns the logical parent of a node\&.
The parent node identifier, or an empty string for the root\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ parent\fP \fIid\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
id
Existing logical node identifier\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
This relationship is independent of the actual Tk widget parent\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Returns the logical parent of a node\&.
The parent node identifier, or an empty string for the root\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBproportions\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Queries or sets all pane proportions of a split\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ proportions\fP \fInode ?weights?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
node
Identifier of an existing split\&.
.TP
weights
Optional list containing one finite positive weight per child, in pane order\&. Omit to query\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Weights are normalized before storage\&. Setting cancels any active deferred drag and schedules geometry
application at idle\&. A query captures current sash positions when geometry is usable and no application is
pending; otherwise it returns the stored proportions\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The normalized list of pane proportions\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBratio\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Queries or sets the first pane fraction of a two-child split\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ ratio\fP \fInode ?value?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
node
Identifier of a split with exactly two children\&.
.TP
value
Optional finite first-pane fraction strictly between zero and one\&. Omit to query\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Use proportions for splits with more children\&. Setting stores the fraction and its complement, cancels a
deferred drag, and schedules idle geometry application\&. Querying captures current geometry when possible,
using the same conditions as proportions\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The stored first pane fraction\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBremove\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Removes a node and all content in its subtree\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ remove\fP \fIid\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
id
Existing node identifier to remove\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Removing the root behaves like clear\&. Otherwise, the parent retains its remaining children with normalized
weights\&. If only one child remains, that child replaces the parent split\&. Surviving content is preserved\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The surviving parent split, its promoted sole child, or the new empty root\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBretain\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Keeps a node while removing its siblings and collapsing its parent\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ retain\fP \fIid\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
id
Existing node identifier to retain\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Destroys all sibling subtrees and their content, then promotes the retained node in place of its immediate
parent\&. Only that parent level is collapsed\&. Retaining the root makes no changes\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The retained node identifier\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBroot\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Returns the current logical root node\&.
The root node identifier\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ root\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Returns the current logical root node\&.
The root node identifier\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBsplit\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Replaces a leaf with a split containing two new leaves\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ split\fP \fInode ?-orient orientation? ?-ratio fraction? ?-keep child?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-keep child
Child receiving the existing content: first or second; default first\&.
.TP
-orient orientation
Split orientation: horizontal or vertical; default horizontal\&.
.TP
-ratio fraction
First child fraction, strictly between zero and one; default 0\&.5\&.
.TP
node
Identifier of the existing leaf to split\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
The original leaf identifier becomes the split identifier, and both child leaves receive new identifiers\&.
The retained content frame and its widget descendants are reused without reparenting or recreation\&. The other
child starts with an empty frame\&. Existing pane proportions are captured before rebuilding the layout\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The two new leaf identifiers in pane order\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBswap\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Exchanges the content frames assigned to two leaves\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ swap\fP \fIa b\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
a
First leaf identifier\&.
.TP
b
Second leaf identifier\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
The leaves can belong to different splits and nesting levels\&. Their logical positions remain unchanged, while
complete content frames and their existing widget state move between those positions\&. Actual Tk parentage and
widget pathnames remain unchanged\&. Equal identifiers do nothing\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Nothing\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBtree\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Returns a recursive snapshot of the logical layout hierarchy\&.
A nested dictionary describing the requested logical subtree\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ tree\fP \fI?id?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
id
Subtree root identifier; empty selects the layout root\&. Optional, default ""\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Each node dictionary contains id, type, parent, widget, and children\&. Leaf dictionaries also contain frame,
with an empty children list\&. Split dictionaries contain orient and proportions; two-child splits also contain
ratio\&. Split children are nested node dictionaries in pane order\&.
.PP
Proportions are refreshed from usable geometry unless application is pending\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Returns a recursive snapshot of the logical layout hierarchy\&.
A nested dictionary describing the requested logical subtree\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBtype\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Returns the type of a logical node\&.
The string leaf or split\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ type\fP \fIid\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
id
Existing logical node identifier\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Returns the type of a logical node\&.
The string leaf or split\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBwidget\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Returns the widget associated with a logical node\&.
The content frame pathname for a leaf, or panedwindow pathname for a split\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ widget\fP \fIid\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
id
Existing logical node identifier\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Returns the widget associated with a logical node\&.
The content frame pathname for a leaf, or panedwindow pathname for a split\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBwidgets\fR (::splitlayout::splitlayout)
.RE
.PP
Returns a recursive snapshot of the actual Tk widget hierarchy\&.
A nested widget dictionary with path, parent, class, manager, container, and children\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSPLITLAYOUTOBJ widgets\fP \fI?path?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
path
Widget subtree root; empty selects the layout hull\&. Optional, default ""\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
The pathname must exist and be the hull or one of its Tk descendants\&. This hierarchy includes application
widgets and is independent of the logical tree returned by tree\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Returns a recursive snapshot of the actual Tk widget hierarchy\&.
A nested widget dictionary with path, parent, class, manager, container, and children\&.


.SH SEE ALSO
splitlayout(n) - package's main page
.br
.sp 1
Public commands and classes documentation:
.br
splitlayout-splitlayout(n)